, August 18, 2026. Colorado is also addressing ozone\npollution through state policies. For more information about\nhealth impacts and how ozone pollution forms in Colorado, visit:\nhttps://cdphe.colorado.gov/ozone- pollution-and-your-health\n\nHEALTH INFORMATION...Increasing likelihood of respiratory symptoms\nand breathing discomfort in active children and adults and people\nwith lung disease, such as asthma. Active children and adults, and\npeople with lung disease, such as asthma, should reduce prolonged\nor heavy outdoor exertion.","ends":"2026-08-18T16:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Broomfield, CO; Adams, CO; Larimer, CO; Jefferson, CO; Denver, CO; Boulder, CO; Weld, CO; Arapahoe, CO; Douglas, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.29db7d75e717a3fee3b2dbc6474566b8c1f30705.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.29db7d75e717a3fee3b2dbc6474566b8c1f30705.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-18T11:49:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 181149 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 549 AM MDT Tue Aug 18 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Scattered showers and thunderstorms expected today and Wednesday. Isolated severe thunderstorm threat both afternoons and evenings. - Above normal temperatures through the weekend. Drier Thursday and Friday, but some monsoonal moisture likely returns by th","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-18T08:47:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Today and tonight... A weak cold front will move through the area late this morning and early afternoon. Impact on temperatures will be minimal, but moisture will increase behind the front. Scattered showers and thunderstorms are forecast for this afternoon through the late evening. A few of these storms could become strong to severe. LONG TERM DISCUSSION...Wednesday through Saturday","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov